Title: ticket-only PRs carry a self-closing Ticket close claim on the ticket they create
Created: 2026-11-09
Author: haduong

--- log ---
2026-11-09T19:17Z haduong created
2026-11-09T20:23Z reviewer raid 4afdb3 verify+reimagine 2026-11-09: see '## Verify and Imagine'; premise checked by reproduction, author decisions listed there; not executed

--- body ---
## Context

Found by the 14-repo housekeeping sweep of 2026-11-09 (19:05-19:15 UTC, run
from the ~/CNRS session). The ticket-only PRs that the harness 1481
native-prune rollout filed in adopter repos carry a `**Ticket:** NNNN` line
naming the very ticket the PR creates. The `/merge` close step runs
`erg close` on the ticket named by `**Ticket:**`, so landing such a PR by the
merge skill closes the new ticket at birth with its exit criteria unmet.

## Evidence

- fuzzy-corpus #74 and sen-causal-reading #171: merged, after review seats
  rewrote the line to `Ticket-ref:` by hand.
- chemin-de-voix #185 (ticket 0262): open, blocked on the close claim.
- padme #258 (ticket 0112): open, blocked on the close claim.
- AEDIST-technical-report #1198: open, blocked on the close claim, and it
  also reuses ticket number 0690 already on main, so it conflicts add/add on
  `tickets/.claims/0690`.

## Diagnosis

Established: the five PRs above carry `**Ticket:**` on the ticket they create
(two repaired by hand, three still open). Not established: which step of the
1481 filing flow writes the line (template, script or agent prompt), and how
the AEDIST PR picked a number already claimed on main (stale base or no
`erg next-id` against origin).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The ticket-filing flow writes `Ticket-ref:`, not `**Ticket:**`, on a PR that creates the ticket
- [ ] chemin-de-voix #185, padme #258 and AEDIST-technical-report #1198 are repaired (close claim rewritten; AEDIST renumbered off 0690)
- [ ] A test covers the filing flow's PR-body line

## Verify and Imagine (raid 4afdb3, 2026-11-09)
- Verified: no harness file writes the filing PR's `**Ticket:**` line; the 1481 executor wrote the
  bodies freehand (journal 2026-11-09-raid-829e9e). Since filing: Tracing-Kieu #185, padme #258 and
  AEDIST #1198 are MERGED with Ticket-ref (19:56-19:59Z; AEDIST renumbered 0691, merge subject still
  says 0690). Criterion 2 met by events. Not listed: climate-finance-het #2050 still OPEN with
  `**Ticket:** tickets/2831-...`, the sixth PR of the flow; its repair is that repo's session's.
- AEDIST duplicate number: `erg new`'s next-id scan timed out and the executor kept 0690 (journal),
  not a stale base; a separate below-floor defect, noted here, not filed.
- Blind-Spot: a guard refusing any `**Ticket:**` claim on a ticket file the same PR adds would block
  legitimate file-and-close PRs (five of the last 100 harness merges: #2336, #2325, #2323, #2272,
  #2242). merge step 1 already stops on a claimed ticket absent from main (SKILL.md:143); check
  whether that is what blocked the three PRs. If so the ticket shrinks to one rule line in
  skills/merge/references/claims.md ("a PR that only files a ticket uses Ticket-ref"); a guard, if
  still wanted, applies only when every file the PR touches is a ticket file.
- Author decisions: (1) criteria 1 and 3 target a filing flow that has no template: reword to a
  rule line plus a narrow guard, or drop the guard; (2) add #2050 to criterion 2.
